---
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';
---

<Figure
  title="Proving you know x without revealing it"
  caption="A toy Schnorr proof over a tiny group (p = 23, order q = 11, g = 4): the prover knows a secret x with y = g^x. Run a round: commit, challenge, respond, verify. Then try a cheating prover who does not know x. The response s = r + c·x is masked by the fresh random r, so it reveals nothing about x on its own."
>
  <schnorr-zkp>
    <div class="ctl-row">
      <label class="stat">Secret x <input type="range" min="1" max="10" value="7" data-x /> <b data-xv>7</b></label>
      <span class="stat" data-pub></span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctl-row">
      <button class="btn primary" data-run="honest">Honest prover: run a round</button>
      <button class="btn primary" data-run="cheat">Cheater (doesn't know x): run a round</button>
    </div>
    <ol class="sz-log" data-log></ol>
    <p class="sz-msg" data-msg aria-live="polite"></p>
  </schnorr-zkp>
</Figure>

<style>
  .sz-log {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.4em;
    font: 0.75rem/1.9 var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    min-height: 7em;
  }
  .sz-log :global(.ok) {
    color: var(--g-green-l);
  }
  .sz-log :global(.no) {
    color: var(--g-red-l);
  }
  .sz-msg {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    min-height: 3em;
  }
  input[type='range'] {
    width: 120px;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
</style>

<script>
  const P = 23;
  const Q = 11;
  const G = 4;
  const pw = (b: number, e: number) => {
    let r = 1;
    for (let i = 0; i < e; i++) r = (r * b) % P;
    return r;
  };
  const rnd = (lo: number, hi: number) => lo + Math.floor(Math.random() * (hi - lo + 1));
  class SchnorrZkp extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      this.querySelector('[data-x]')!.addEventListener('input', () => this.pub());
      this.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-run]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => this.run(b.dataset.run === 'honest')));
      this.pub();
    }
    x() {
      return +this.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-x]')!.value;
    }
    pub() {
      this.querySelector('[data-xv]')!.textContent = String(this.x());
      this.querySelector('[data-pub]')!.innerHTML = `public key y = 4^${this.x()} mod 23 = <b>${pw(G, this.x())}</b>`;
      this.querySelector('[data-log]')!.innerHTML = '';
      this.querySelector('[data-msg]')!.textContent = 'The verifier knows only y. Run a round.';
    }
    run(honest: boolean) {
      const y = pw(G, this.x());
      const r = rnd(1, Q - 1);
      const t = pw(G, r);
      const c = rnd(1, Q - 1);
      // an honest prover answers s = r + c*x; a cheater does not know x, so after seeing c it can only guess s
      const s = honest ? (r + c * this.x()) % Q : rnd(0, Q - 1);
      const lhs = pw(G, s);
      const rhs = (t * pw(y, c)) % P;
      const ok = lhs === rhs;
      this.querySelector('[data-log]')!.innerHTML = [
        `prover commits: t = g^r = 4^${r} mod 23 = <b>${t}</b>  (r is random and stays secret)`,
        `verifier challenges: c = <b>${c}</b>  (random)`,
        `prover responds: s = ${honest ? 'r + c·x mod 11' : 'a guess (does not know x)'} = <b>${s}</b>`,
        `verifier checks g^s = ${lhs}  vs  t · y^c = ${t} · ${y}^${c} = ${rhs}  →  <span class="${ok ? 'ok' : 'no'}">${ok ? 'ACCEPT' : 'REJECT'}</span>`,
      ].map((l) => `<li>${l}</li>`).join('');
      this.querySelector('[data-msg]')!.textContent = honest
        ? 'Completeness: an honest prover always passes, because g^s = g^(r+cx) = g^r · (g^x)^c = t · y^c. The verifier saw t, c and s, but s is hidden by the random r, so x is not revealed.'
        : ok
          ? 'The cheater got lucky: its guessed response happened to be right, which in this tiny group happens 1 time in 11. Real groups are enormous (and proofs repeat), so the chance becomes negligible.'
          : 'Soundness: after seeing the challenge, a prover without x cannot compute the right response, so it is rejected (except for a 1/11 lucky guess here). Press the cheater button a few times to see an occasional pass.';
    }
  }
  customElements.define('schnorr-zkp', SchnorrZkp);
</script>
